  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang clan’s first and second supreme elders weigh Suan Bu Jin and Old Ghost Bai Jun as obstacles in green ghost desert. Fragmented Qing clan inheritance clues, pieced together over generations, already name Immortal Gu House Divine Bean Palace, and Fang clan’s resolve to take it has been carried across generations.",
      "chapters": [
        1507
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_fang_clan",
        "char_old_ghost_bai_jun",
        "inh_qing_clan_inheritance",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Old Ghost Bai Jun and Eagle Concubine later enter a green-lit space beneath a quicksand pit, climb a golden staircase, and kneel before a lofty palace whose plaque reads Divine Bean Palace. Inside, an enormous soul beast with tortoise shell, tiger paws, dragon tail, snake neck, and human head lies in the hall; green rays from the palace pierce it when it rages, and it curses the house that restrains it. In Heavenly Court, Fairy Zi Wei reads a green aurora as involving Genesis Lotus Immortal Venerable, names Divine Bean Palace a rank eight Immortal Gu House about to appear, and sends Heavenly Lotus Sect first supreme elder Chen Yi to subdue it before Western Desert can claim it.",
      "chapters": [
        1508
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_eagle_concubine",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "char_genesis_lotus_immortal_venerable",
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect",
        "char_chen_yi",
        "reg_western_desert"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When the house assaults Fang Yuan and Fang clan’s Fallen Flower Hall, Fang Yuan and the Fang clan immortals recognize the rank eight Immortal Gu House Divine Bean Palace on sight. Its charge snaps a winged black python immemorial soul beast in two and chips the palace itself.",
      "chapters": [
        1515
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "palace-assault",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "house_fallen_flower_hall"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chen Yi’s karma divine tree reading places Genesis Lotus in Western Desert three hundred thousand years ago. After a child’s plea to revive his mother, Genesis Lotus leaves Divine Bean Palace in a village well; the village is buried, the house passes among mortals, and Qing clan obtains it. Spectral Soul, not yet a venerable, slaughters Qing clan; Qing clan’s first supreme elder seals the clan inheritance inside Divine Bean Palace. Soul fragments gather there and form the legendary immemorial soul beast Qing Chou, which is born from the palace and imprisoned in it. Over ages Qing Chou learns to force the rank eight house for a time and open an entrance; Old Ghost Bai Jun and Eagle Concubine enter and become its slaves.",
      "chapters": [
        1516
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "origin-and-holders",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_qing_clan",
        "char_qing_chou"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chen Yi judges that Qing Chou, trapped inside, cannot use the house’s full power, and that Fang clan’s Chicken Dog Coop and Inquiry Dock joining Fallen Flower Hall would form the battlefield killer move peach blossom maze.",
      "chapters": [
        1518
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "limited-house-control",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_chicken_dog_coop",
        "house_inquiry_dock"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chen Yi notes divine bean soldiers as a product the palace can raise, though in that fight he can only rely on a soul beast army instead.",
      "chapters": [
        1523
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "divine-bean-soldiers",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the battle, Fang clan obtains Divine Bean Palace, though the house is nearly half destroyed, Chicken Dog Coop and Inquiry Dock are heavily damaged, and first supreme elder Fang Gong is badly hurt. Fang clan expects Western Desert super forces to contest the gain once news spreads that they hold the house.",
      "chapters": [
        1530
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_gong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Divine Bean Palace is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-aftermath",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
